The first age of the dungeon was one of silence.
No torches burned in the deep corridors.
The builders carved their secrets into stone,
hoping that only the worthy would find them.

They spoke of a great library, hidden below
the lowest chamber, where knowledge was kept
safe from the ravages of time and war.

The archivists wore cloaks of grey and spoke
in whispers, for the tomes were sacred to them.

RUNE: ARCANE

Many who entered the archives never returned,
lost among the endless shelves and winding paths.
Some say the library itself is alive,
shifting its corridors to confuse intruders.

The first rune was said to hold the power
of ancient magic, known only to the builders.
Those who spoke its name could bend light
and shadow to their will.

Beware the false runes that glow with dim light,
for they lead only to dead ends and dust.

The archivists kept careful records of every
tome, organized by subject and by author.
But the system was lost when the last archivist
vanished into the deeper chambers below.
